<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Confederation of the Rhine</h1><p class="st-meta">1806 CE – 1813 CE · capital Frankfurt am Main</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Napoleon's league of German client states, whose creation in 1806 brought the end of the Holy Roman Empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 12 July 1806 sixteen German states, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, Württemberg and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a>, signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine-confederation-act">Rhine Confederation Act</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, leaving the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon's</a> protection. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Emperor Francis II</a> abdicated as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> on 6 August 1806. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a> and many smaller states joined later, bringing it to some 39 members.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> was its protector and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-theodor-von-dalberg">Karl Theodor von Dalberg</a> its prince-primate. A federal diet in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> was planned but never met. Members were bound to a military alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and had to supply contingents, notably for the 1812 Russian campaign. Within their borders many states introduced Napoleonic reforms, ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a> and absorbed mediatised lands.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon's</a> defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a> in October 1813, its members changed sides one by one and the confederation dissolved. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> replaced it in 1815 with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/confederation-of-the-rhine.jpg" alt="Confederation of the Rhine" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: TRAJAN 117 This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Confederation_of_the_Rhine_(1812).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1806 CE – 1813 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Frankfurt am Main</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Napoleon I, Karl Theodor von Dalberg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>, <a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a>, <a href="/countries/liechtenstein">Liechtenstein</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rheinbund, Rhenish Confederation</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=confederation-of-the-rhine" aria-label="Confederation of the Rhine on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4879 435 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Confederation of the Rhine lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5199 691L5229 694M5199 691L5269 749M5199 691L5312 664M5199 691L5257 666M5199 691L5244 667M5199 691L5251 687M5199 691L5279 723M5199 691L5198 698M5199 691L5189 692M5199 691L5173 680M5199 691L5149 641M5199 691L5107 669M5199 691L5212 730M5199 691L5194 723M5199 691L5208 743M5199 691L5214 751M5199 691L5184 744M5199 691L5200 638M5199 691L5223 779M5199 691L5054 728M5199 691L5199 691M5199 691L5215 656M5199 691L5154 659M5199 691L5199 691M5199 691L5228